        "original_id": "c3b6cf53-0f7d-5bc1-a5d7-584af2ef230e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Chinese Crested Dog, Chien-gris, Mexican Hairless Dog\n- Concepts: Hairless dog breeds, Powderpuff, Hairless, alopecia, canine follicular dysplasia\n\nFacts:\n- Chien-gris, also called Gris de Saint-Louis, was a dog breed that originated in Medieval times and is now extinct.\n- The Chinese Crested Dog is a hairless breed of dog.\n- The Chinese Crested Dog has two varieties born in the same litter: the Powderpuff, which has fur, and the Hairless, which does not.\n- The Mexican Hairless Dog and the Chinese Crested Dog are among breeds specifically bred for alopecia.",
